<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">29 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 29 October, from 312 to 2012.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-i" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantine-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">312 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,714 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Constantine I enters Rome after his victory at the Milvian Bridge</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A day after defeating Maxentius at the Milvian Bridge, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-i">Constantine I</a> entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in a grand adventus met with jubilation. He promised to restore the Senate's ancestral privileges, and there was no revenge against Maxentius' supporters.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-i">Constantine I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1268">1268 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">758 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Conradin, the last Hohenstaufen, is beheaded in Naples</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conradin">Conradin</a>, the last legitimate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a>, who at fifteen had invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> to recover <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-anjou">Charles of Anjou</a>, was beheaded in the market square of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> after his defeat at Tagliacozzo and capture while fleeing.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conradin">Conradin</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1281 CE <span class="tih-ago">745 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Mamluks defeat the Ilkhanate at the Second Battle of Homs</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, the armies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a> defeated those of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>, a division of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a> centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. The battle was part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abaqa-khan">Abaqa Khan</a>'s attempt to take Syria from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egyptians">Egyptians</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1618">1618 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">408 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sir Walter Raleigh is beheaded at Westminster</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Courtier, poet and explorer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walter-raleigh">Sir Walter Raleigh</a> was executed in Old Palace Yard under a treason sentence from 1603. James I revived it after Raleigh's failed expedition to Guiana attacked a Spanish settlement.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1787">1787 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">239 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mozart's Don Giovanni premieres in Prague</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mozart conducted the first performance of Don Giovanni at the Estates <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>. The opera, with a libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte, blends comedy and the supernatural and is ranked among the greatest ever written.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1863">1863 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">163 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A Geneva conference founds the Red Cross movement</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An international conference called by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> committee of Henri Dunant closed by adopting resolutions for national relief societies for wounded soldiers. The Red Cross movement and the 1864 Geneva Convention followed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1929">1929 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">97 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Black Tuesday: the Wall Street Crash deepens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">More than 16 million shares were sold in a day of panic on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Stock Exchange. Black Tuesday became the emblem of the crash that preceded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-depression">Great Depression</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2012">2012 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">14 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hurricane Sandy makes landfall in New Jersey</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Sandy came ashore near Atlantic City, bringing a record storm surge that flooded lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan">Manhattan</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> subway. Across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> it killed more than 230 people.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 29 October <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/franz-von-papen"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/franz-von-papen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Franz von Papen</span><span class="tp">1879–1969</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/joseph-goebbels"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/joseph-goebbels.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Joseph Goebbels</span><span class="tp">1897–1945</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ellen-johnson-sirleaf"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ellen-johnson-sirleaf.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ellen Johnson Sirleaf</span><span class="tp">b. 1938</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-magufuli"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-magufuli.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Magufuli</span><span class="tp">1959–2021</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 29 October <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/conradin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/conradin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Conradin</span><span class="tp">1252–1268</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/stefan-milutin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/stefan-milutin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Stefan Milutin</span><span class="tp">c. 1253–1321</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/walter-raleigh"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/walter-raleigh.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Walter Raleigh</span><span class="tp">c. 1552–1618</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
